when you decide to opt for an mba  program the first big step would be to  get a high gmat score  this is because your admission into the  top p schools depends on your gmat score  so in this video we will reflect on all  the essential information you need to  know about this crucial yet dreaded test  but before we begin make sure to  subscribe to our channel and hit the  bell icon to never miss an update from  simplylearn gmat is the acronym for  graduate management admission test the  purpose of this test is to measure your  aptitude for management education  this test is an adaptive computer  assessment which means that the degree  of difficulty for each question will  depend on how you performed in the  previous questions  gmat grades are typically valid for five  years and the examination cost is 250 us  dollars  this exam can be attempted five times a  year and totally eight times throughout  your lifetime  the graduate management admission  council administers this examination  thus these scores are accepted by a  large number of universities across the  globe there are almost 7 000 programs at  approximately 2 300 b schools that  accept gmat scores for mba mim and other  management related programs  it is crucial for you to ace gmat test  since a high gmat score will not only  get you into your dream management  program and institution but it can also  enhance your chances of getting good  scholarships  having said that let's discuss the gmat  exam format  gmat takes three hours and seven minutes  to solve if you take no breaks in  between the sections however gmat  permits you to take two eight minute  breaks between the quant verbal and  integrated reasoning sections  this test assesses your ability to  perform in typical managerial roles if  you think what aptitude and verbal  skills have to do with it then think  about this  a manager is expected to be able to  manage two things people and numbers and  what better way to do it than to put  your aptitude and linguistic skills to  the test  gmat will test you in overall four  sections  integrated reasoning quantitative  analysis  verbal reasoning and analytical writing  assessment or awa  in the awa section you will have to  determine the reasoning behind the  provided argument and write a critique  of it including appropriate examples and  explanations  the ir section is designed to test your  analytical skills to solve complex  problems  here you will be provided with data in  various forms  by processing and extracting relevant  data you will be able to choose the  right answers for questions under this  section  the next section is verbal reasoning  in this section you will come across  reading comprehension critical reasoning  and sentence correction questions  your grammatical and linguistic  knowledge will be tested thoroughly in  this section  the last and fourth section of gmat is  quantitative ability  this section will put your mathematical  skills to test  most of the time the more thought of  having to deal with mathematics causes  us to despair but don't let this disturb  you as the mathematics involved in gmat  is what you have learnt at your high  school stage you just need to be clear  on the basics and then the rest is all  about implementing the skills you've  learned  this section has 31 questions and you'll  have two minutes to answer each of these  questions this portion of quants is  further split into three sections  arithmetic algebra and geometry  number theory percentage fractions  simple and compound interest set theory  rational and proportion speed time and  distance mixture and allegations  probability are all covered in the  arithmetic section  algebra contains sub-topics such as  permutations and combinations quadratic  equations  inequalities and basic statistics and  also algebraic expressions  and the geometry section deals with  topics such as quadrilaterals cylinders  coordinate geometry trigonometry and  solid shapes  all of the above mentioned topics must  have been covered in your high schools  right hence you will only need plenty of  practice to get a perfect score in this  section of gmat  the verbal and quantitative sections  contribute to the total score of 800.  each of these sessions is assessed on a  scale of 6 to 51 points while the  overall result is graded on a scale of  200 to 800 marks  the remaining two components awa and  integrated reasoning receive their  independent scores the next question we  have is  when and how to attempt the gmat test  you can take the gmat at more than 700  test centers across the globe you will  have to identify the closest test center  to your region and register the details  along with the date and time  many students delay it till a few months  before the application deadline  that's a terrible idea  to be on the safer side take at least  one year prior to your application date  that way you'll have plenty of time to  retake it if needed now the last topic  we have for this discussion is how to  prepare for gmat when it comes to gmat  preparation you have a number of  alternatives there are several coaching  institutions that can equip you to  perform to your full potential in the  gmat exam  these offliner online coaching crash  courses equipped with mock tests doubt  solving sessions and post entrance  assistance can undoubtedly help you  create your own strategy to get into  your dream management program  however self-study is the most cost  effective and adaptable method of  preparation  there are a plethora of kojima books  available to assist you in covering  everything from fundamentals to the  advanced topics the best gmat book that  you can refer to is the gmat official  guide  the graduate management admission  council publishes it on a yearly basis  by brushing up the understanding of  basic concepts and practicing over  multiple problems  you can definitely accomplish a good  gmat score  the average time necessity to complete  gmat study is about 3 months  of course a lot will rely on how quickly  you can learn the fundamentals and the  mode of study you choose for preparation  that's all we have for today i wish you  all the very best for your gmat test  thank you for watching this video and  stay tuned for more from simplylearn  hi there if you like this video  subscribe to the simply learn youtube  channel and click here to watch similar  videos turn it up and get certified  click here
 

